 "notes": {
  "method": "D03 (cam (210.0,67.5), looking SSE ~164 deg at the NW chamfered corner (215.0,56.5)-(211.8,53.7)): a single tall storey (~5.5-6 m) of rough honey ashlar with tall round-arched openings (teal boarded door with a radial fanlight on the chamfer, dark-red and green doors), a deep maroon steel canopy on iron hoop brackets wrapping the corner at ~3.6-4.2 m, and a low red-tile hipped roof (also seen in front of the St John dome in D02). The chamfer edges are under 2.4 m, so their openings cannot be built; edges 7 (north, 23 m) and 2 (west) carry the row.",
  "roof": "hipped: the footprint is nearly rectangular (bounding-box overhang ~8 %)"
